# bootstrap-ssh — SSH certificate authority public key(s) to trust.
#
# This is the *CA's* public key: the .pub file sitting next to the private key
# you sign certificates with. It is NOT your certificate.
#
#   ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... my-ssh-ca
#
# A certificate only carries its issuer's fingerprint, not the issuer's key, so
# the CA key cannot be recovered from a cert — it has to be copied here.
# Get it from the CA host with:  cat /path/to/ssh_ca.pub
#
# Every certificate this CA signed is then accepted, until it expires or the
# principal no longer matches. One line per CA; blank lines and # are ignored.
